#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-difftool(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:7
msgid "git-difftool - Show changes using common diff tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:12
msgid "'git difftool' [<options>] [<commit> [<commit>]] [--] [<path>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:19
msgid ""
"'git difftool' is a Git command that allows you to compare and edit files "
"between revisions using common diff tools.  'git difftool' is a frontend to "
"'git diff' and accepts the same options and arguments. See "
"linkgit:git-diff[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-d`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--dir-diff`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Copy the modified files to a temporary location and perform a directory diff "
"on them. This mode never prompts before launching the diff tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-y`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-prompt`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:31
msgid "Do not prompt before launching a diff tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--prompt`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:36
msgid ""
"Prompt before each invocation of the diff tool.  This is the default "
"behaviour; the option is provided to override any configuration settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--rotate-to=<file>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Start showing the diff for the given path, the paths before it will move to "
"the end and output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--skip-to=<file>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:44
msgid "Start showing the diff for the given path, skipping all the paths before it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-t <tool>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--tool=<tool>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:50
msgid ""
"Use the diff tool specified by <tool>.  Valid values include emerge, "
"kompare, meld, and vimdiff. Run `git difftool --tool-help` for the list of "
"valid <tool> settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:55
msgid ""
"If a diff tool is not specified, 'git difftool' will use the configuration "
"variable `diff.tool`.  If the configuration variable `diff.tool` is not set, "
"'git difftool' will pick a suitable default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:61
msgid ""
"You can explicitly provide a full path to the tool by setting the "
"configuration variable `difftool.<tool>.path`. For example, you can "
"configure the absolute path to kdiff3 by setting "
"`difftool.kdiff3.path`. Otherwise, 'git difftool' assumes the tool is "
"available in PATH."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Instead of running one of the known diff tools, 'git difftool' can be "
"customized to run an alternative program by specifying the command line to "
"invoke in a configuration variable `difftool.<tool>.cmd`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:76
msgid ""
"When 'git difftool' is invoked with this tool (either through the `-t` or "
"`--tool` option or the `diff.tool` configuration variable)  the configured "
"command line will be invoked with the following variables available: "
"`$LOCAL` is set to the name of the temporary file containing the contents of "
"the diff pre-image and `$REMOTE` is set to the name of the temporary file "
"containing the contents of the diff post-image.  `$MERGED` is the name of "
"the file which is being compared. `$BASE` is provided for compatibility with "
"custom merge tool commands and has the same value as `$MERGED`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--tool-help`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:79
msgid "Print a list of diff tools that may be used with `--tool`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--symlinks`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-symlinks`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:86
msgid ""
"'git difftool''s default behavior is to create symlinks to the working tree "
"when run in `--dir-diff` mode and the right-hand side of the comparison "
"yields the same content as the file in the working tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:89
msgid ""
"Specifying `--no-symlinks` instructs 'git difftool' to create copies "
"instead.  `--no-symlinks` is the default on Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-x <command>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--extcmd=<command>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:96
msgid ""
"Specify a custom command for viewing diffs.  'git-difftool' ignores the "
"configured defaults and runs `<command> $LOCAL $REMOTE` when this option is "
"specified.  Additionally, `$BASE` is set in the environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-g`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--gui`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-gui`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:108
msgid ""
"When 'git-difftool' is invoked with the `-g` or `--gui` option the default "
"diff tool will be read from the configured `diff.guitool` variable instead "
"of `diff.tool`. This may be selected automatically using the configuration "
"variable `difftool.guiDefault`. The `--no-gui` option can be used to "
"override these settings. If `diff.guitool` is not set, we will fallback in "
"the order of `merge.guitool`, `diff.tool`, `merge.tool` until a tool is "
"found."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--trust-exit-code`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-trust-exit-code`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:114
msgid ""
"Errors reported by the diff tool are ignored by default.  Use "
"`--trust-exit-code` to make 'git-difftool' exit when an invoked diff tool "
"returns a non-zero exit code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:117
msgid ""
"'git-difftool' will forward the exit code of the invoked tool when "
"`--trust-exit-code` is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:119
msgid "See linkgit:git-diff[1] for the full list of supported options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-difftool.adoc:124
msgid ""
"'git difftool' falls back to 'git mergetool' config variables when the "
"difftool equivalents have not been defined."
msgstr ""

